# Chromium · Cr · gate 24

**Chromium** (Cr) is element **24** of the periodic table — a **transition metal**, period 4, group 6, d-block, solid at standard conditions, atomic weight **51.996**.

## The element (carbon layer — reference chemistry)
The shine of chrome; turns steel stainless; the green of emerald and the red of ruby.

## The gate (silicon layer — the 118 Gates)
Under David Wise's four-state cycle, gate **24** falls on **1:1** because (Z−1) mod 4 = **3**. That state is *the held balance — fully manifest, matched, made — born of the world* — the nature of emergence here is **natural**. Chromium is not a thing apart; it is the one stochastic element, caught at this beat of its cycle.

## Emergence — natural
This emergent carries the **natural** nature: the same four — natural · ethereal · spiritual · electrical — that run through every sphere of UD0. Its color is `#5fae7a`.

